--- Comment #10 from Suharto Anggono (suharto_anggono@yahoo.com) ---
With r90446, `dim2total` ends with

```
#ifdef LONG_VECTOR_SUPPORT
    if (dn &gt; R_XLEN_T_MAX)
#else
    if (dn &gt; INT_MAX)
#endif
        *err = true;
    return (R_xlen_t) dn;
```

So, `(R_xlen_t) dn` is also returned if `dn &gt; R_XLEN_T_MAX`.

`(R_xlen_t) dn` has undefined behavior if `dn` value cannot be represented by
`R_xlen_t`.

It is better for `dn &gt; R_XLEN_T_MAX` case to return separately. For example,

```
#ifdef LONG_VECTOR_SUPPORT
    if (dn &gt; R_XLEN_T_MAX)
#else
    if (dn &gt; INT_MAX)
#endif
        {*err = true; return 0;}
    return (R_xlen_t) dn;
```

